==== Install Instructions: ====

=== Serial + initramfs: ===
  - Place OpenWrt initramfs image for the device on a TFTP in the server's root. This example uses Server IP: 192.168.1.3
  - Connect serial console (115200,8n1) to [[#serial|X8 connector]].
  - Connect TFTP host to MF286D using an ethernet cable. Don't use the shared WAN/LAN1 port. 
  - Stop u-Boot by pressing ESC, and run u-Boot commands: <code>
setenv serverip 192.168.1.3
setenv ipaddr 192.168.1.72
set fdt_high 0x85000000
tftp openwrt-ipq40xx-generic-zte_mf286d-initramfs-fit-zImage.itb
bootm $loadaddr</code>
  - If you want to be able to revert to stock, make backup of original partitions, it's documented on the [[:toh:zte:mf286r#step_2backing_up_original_software|MF286R page]].
  - Login via ssh or serial and use wget (or any other utility) to download sysupgrade image into 'tmp/'. You may skip this and instead do it through LuCI web interface later.
  - Remove stock partitions:<code>
ubiattach -m 9 #it could return error if ubi was attached before or rootfs part was erased before
ubirmvol /dev/ubi0 -N ubi_rootfs #it could return error if rootfs part was erased before
ubirmvol /dev/ubi0 -N ubi_rootfs_data #some devices doesn't have it</code>
  - If installing from sysupgrade image stored at 'tmp/', proceed to install image via "sysupgrade -n" (like "sysupgrade -n tmp/openwrt-ipq40xx-generic-zte_mf286d-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin"; previously retrieved image using wget). Sometimes it could print ubi attach error, but please ignore it if process goes forward.
  - If during the install you get:<code>ubi0 warning: 0xc070b5d0: error -74 (ECC error) while reading 64 bytes from PEB 169:2048, read only 64 bytes, retry</code> Or on reboot it fails and leaves you on uboot with <code>Nand Flash error. Status = 12336 NAND page read failed</code> Then /dev/mtd9 needs to be formatted.
  - Boot with the factory image again (as listed above) and use issue the following followed by the sysupgrade:<code>
ubidetach -m 9
ubiformat -y /dev/mtd9
sysupgrade -n openwrt.......bin</code>
  - If installing from LuCI, make sure sysupgrade image is on your computer. While computer is connected to router through Ethernet cable, within your browser go to [[http://openwrt.lan]] (see [[docs:guide-quick-start:walkthrough_login|this]] for alternative ways) and you'll see login page, leave password blank and press 'Login'. Follow [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.sysupgrade#for_luci-based_upgrades|this guide]] for further steps.


