===== Basic configuration =====
Since the router is equipped with LTE modem as its main WAN interface, it might be useful to connect to the Internet right away after installation. To do so over Luci, you'd need to connect to the Internet via other means (Ethernet or Wi-Fi STA) and then install ''luci-proto-qmi'' package.

You can also add the necessary packages when building a new image with [[https://firmware-selector.openwrt.org/|Firmware Selector]] or download the package(s) via OpenWrt's website (architecture: arm_cortex-a7_neon-vfpv4), upload them to the router and install manually, which doesn't require the router to be connected to the Internet. As of this writing, the package can be found from the following page (check and update the version accordingly): https://downloads.openwrt.org/releases/23.05.5/packages/arm_cortex-a7_neon-vfpv4/luci/

If you can't access the Internet via other means or you want to set it up via console or SSH, you can put the following entries in ''/etc/config/network'', replacing the specific APN with one needed for your ISP.

<code>
config interface 'wwan'
        option proto 'qmi'
        option device '/dev/cdc-wdm0'
        option pdptype 'IP'
        option apn 'internet'
</code>

Please refer to [[:docs:guide-user:network:wan:wwan:ltedongle#configuration|QMI modem configuration]] for further details.
 
After configuring your LTE modem, you can follow [[docs:guide-user:base-system:start|Basic configuration]] to proceed with other configuration steps, such as [[:docs:guide-user:network:wifi:start|setting up your Wi-Fi]].

